# L §8.3 Which refusal prints (tally 2.1.1): load splits every file into lines and tokens before it parses any. a.tally
# comes first by its path and its grammar fails on line 4; b.tally's line 5 holds a tab, which the split refuses: the
# tab prints, since the split of every file comes before the parse of any.
=== z.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
=== a.tally
part pa
  tally 2

def y int 1
=== b.tally
part pb
  tally 2

def x: int = 1
	def w: int = 2
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PARSE cannot parse: tab (b.tally:5)
